# Frozen eval fixtures whose BYTE identity is asserted by a test.
#
# This repo runs with core.autocrlf=true, so by default git rewrites LF to CRLF
# in the working tree on checkout. For a file whose bytes are compared against a
# freshly generated copy, that conversion makes the test fail on a clean clone
# for a reason that has nothing to do with the file's contents -- and the
# tempting "fix" is to regenerate the fixture, which is exactly how a real drift
# would get buried (see docs/HANDOFF-development.md on byte-identity fixtures).
#
# `-text` tells git to do no end-of-line conversion on these paths at all, so
# what the builder writes is what every checkout gets.
evals/_layers_regression_sample.jsonl -text
